Untangled is split-licensed. There is no single license for the whole
repository: each top-level folder carries its own LICENSE file, which governs
every file under that folder.

  Folder          License        SPDX identifier   Text
  ------          -------        ---------------   ----
  php/            MIT            MIT               php/LICENSE
  typescript/     MIT            MIT               typescript/LICENSE
  spec/           MIT            MIT               spec/LICENSE
  conformance/    MIT            MIT               conformance/LICENSE
  docs/           MIT            MIT               docs/LICENSE
  python/         GPL v2 only    GPL-2.0-only      python/LICENSE

Files outside these folders (this file, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, scripts/,
.github/) are licensed under the MIT license (LICENSES/MIT.txt).

Why the split: python/ may port code from Martin Blais's snakefood
(https://github.com/blais/snakefood), which is distributed under the GNU
General Public License version 2. A port or translation of that code is a
derivative work and must stay under the GPL, so it lives only in python/.
Everything else is new work, published under the permissive MIT license.
GPL-licensed code must never be copied into an MIT folder.

Each package also declares its license in its own metadata (composer.json,
package.json, pyproject.toml), and source files carry an SPDX header such as

  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

scripts/check-licenses.sh verifies in CI that every header matches its folder.

The full license texts are in LICENSES/:

  LICENSES/MIT.txt
  LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt

Contributions take the license of the folder they land in. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
